From: w2xg2022 <w2xg2022@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: dts: guard CONFIG_SYS_SPI_U_BOOT_OFFS in rockchip-u-boot.dtsi

CONFIG_SYS_SPI_U_BOOT_OFFS lives in common/spl/Kconfig and only has a
default when SPL_SPI_LOAD or SPL_SPI_SUNXI is enabled. Boards that select
ROCKCHIP_SPI_IMAGE (i.e. every rk3288/rk3399 target in
arch/arm/mach-rockchip/*/Kconfig) but keep SPL SPI loading disabled end up
with the token unsubstituted, which breaks the dts build:

    Lexical error: arch/arm/dts/rockchip-u-boot.dtsi:225.14-40 Unexpected 'CONFIG_SYS_SPI_U_BOOT_OFFS'
    FATAL ERROR: Syntax error parsing input tree
    make[2]: *** [scripts/Makefile.lib:482: arch/arm/dts/rk3288-evb.dtb] Error 1

This is hit by rk3288 xt-q8l-v10 (configs/xt-q8l-v10-rk3288_defconfig), which
does not enable SPL SPI load. Guard the property with #ifdef; when the symbol
is defined nothing changes, and when it is not binman falls back to its
default offset for the payload node.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rockchip-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rockchip-u-boot.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rockchip-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rockchip-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -222,7 +222,9 @@
 		u-boot-img {
 #endif
 			/* Sync with u-boot,spl-payload-offset if present */
+#ifdef CONFIG_SYS_SPI_U_BOOT_OFFS
 			offset = <CONFIG_SYS_SPI_U_BOOT_OFFS>;
+#endif
 		};
 	};
 #endif /* CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_SPI_IMAGE */
